      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>This  short text is a list of ṣǝnǝʿt and ṣǝnṣǝnt days of the twelve months (sometimes thirteen, including Ṗagʷǝmen). The text is attested in a large number of manuscripts, most often as an addition. 
               The wording, as well as the number of ṣǝnǝʿt and ṣǝnṣǝnt days in each month, varies considerably across the witnesses. According to <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/ZWRWSGIF"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Grebaut1913Joursfastes"/><title level="a">Les jours fastes et néfastes d’après le ms. éthiopien n° 3 de M. E. Delorme</title><title level="j">Revue de l’Orient Chrétien</title><author><forename>Sylvain</forename><surname>Grébaut</surname></author><date>1913</date><biblScope unit="volume">18</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">97-98</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Grebaut1913Joursfastes</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Grebaut1913Joursfastes</note></t:bibl>, the text is a list of lucky and unlucky days. Following the suggestions by Gasparini in <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/WJIRG8JQ"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Gasparini1946Vocabili"/><title level="a">Di due vocaboli etiopici oscuri</title><title level="j">Rassegna di Studi Etiopici</title><author><forename>P. Armido</forename><surname>Gasparini</surname></author><date>1946</date><biblScope unit="volume">5</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">79-82</biblScope><note type="url">http://www.jstor.org/stable/41465362</note><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">Lexicon</note><note type="tag">South Semitic</note><note type="tag">Vocabulary</note><note type="tag">bm:Gasparini1946Vocabili</note></note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">Lexicon</note><note type="tag">South Semitic</note><note type="tag">Vocabulary</note><note type="tag">bm:Gasparini1946Vocabili</note></t:bibl>, 
               Elagina, in <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/JD2HULC9"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Elagina2025Hassab"/><title level="a">Description of Ḥassāb-Related Material: Ḥassāba Ṣǝnǝʿt wa-Ṣǝnṣǝnt (CAe 4145)</title><title level="j">Rassegna di Studi Etiopici</title><author><forename>Daria</forename><surname>Elagina</surname></author><date>2025</date><biblScope unit="volume">3&lt;sup&gt;a&lt;/sup&gt; Serie, 9</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81-106</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Elagina2025Hassab</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Elagina2025Hassab</note></t:bibl>, argues that the text goes back to the long-standing tradition of moonwood, that is, the determination of days for cutting wood based on lunar phases. 
              </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
